Run the default preset load once per Restore Defaults press

The defaults() slot sets the preset combo box to the (Default) entry.
It then calls setPreset() and kwin->defaults() directly. A combo box
write that changes the index already runs setPreset() through the
currentIndexChanged connection. That run calls kwin->defaults() for
the (Default) entry. In that case the two direct calls repeat the work
of the connection.

A combo box write that holds the index emits no signal. For a press
that starts on the (Default) entry, the direct call is the only preset
load.

The new shape dispatches on the index. The slot calls setPreset()
directly when the combo box already sits on the (Default) entry. The
slot writes the combo box otherwise and lets the connection make the
one call. Each press then runs one preset load and one kwin->defaults()
call.

The change stays inside defaults(). The body of setPreset(), the
connection and the interactive preset path keep their behaviour.

The change sits on the branch work/dialog-state of the local tree, as
commit 13 of 13. The fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request !26
on system/qtcurve holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
index cbdca44f..a682cf9c 100644
--- a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
+++ b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
@@ -1371,9 +1371,10 @@ void QtCurveConfig::defaults()
         if(presetsCombo->itemText(i)==defaultText)
             index=i;
 
-    presetsCombo->setCurrentIndex(index);
-    setPreset();
-    kwin->defaults();
+    if (presetsCombo->currentIndex() == index)
+        setPreset();
+    else
+        presetsCombo->setCurrentIndex(index);
 }
 
 // Reset the options of the shown section to the values of the default
